re-rounding value wins over the true grand total.\",\n    \"image-ocr has no notion of 'post-rounding' total: the presence of a 'ROUNDING' / 'ROUNDING ADJ' line between two candidate totals is not used to prefer the later candidate.\",\n    \"image-ocr date extraction scans the whole text with generic regexes and returns the first well-formed match, with no preference for dates appearing on a line containing a DATE keyword, so stray digit groups elsewhere on the receipt can win.\",\n    \"image-ocr runs a single OCR/preprocessing pass per receipt; a single misread digit (1→7, O→0, etc.) silently produces a confidently-wrong amount with no cross-check against other total-bearing lines on the same receipt.\",\n    \"image-ocr can drop a total entirely when the OCR'd keyword line is slightly garbled and the two-line fallback only looks one line ahead; it then returns None with no second-chance scan of the bottom region of the receipt.\",\n    \"xlsx strict-schema pattern is in the candidate skill but the run still produced an empty string for the failed cell, indicating the guidance is not operationally sticky: missing values need to be materialised as Python None before to_excel, and verified by a re-read that the cell is truly empty.\"\n  ],\n  \"skill_defects\": [\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"defect\": \"extract_total iterates lines top-down and short-circuits on the first match within a tier; it should prefer the LAST match within a tier (totals live at the bottom of receipts) and must prefer a TOTAL match that occurs AFTER any 'ROUNDING' / 'ROUNDING ADJ' line.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"defect\": \"No context rule for 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' vs a later plain 'TOTAL' line; the current tiered keyword list treats them as equivalent even though the plain trailing TOTAL is the grader-aligned value.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"defect\": \"Date extraction has no proximity-to-keyword preference (DATE, DATE:, DATED, PRINT DATE, 'Date :') and no plausibility check (year range, agreement across multiple candidate matches), so a non-date digit cluster can outrank the real date line.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"defect\": \"Multi-pass OCR exists but is not wired into the field extractor: when extract_total fails, when it returns a value that disagrees with the other total-bearing lines on the same receipt, or when the two-line fallback is hit, the pipeline does not retry with alternate PSM / preprocessing variants.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"defect\": \"Two-line fallback only looks at the single next line; it does not scan forward a small window (2–3 lines) for the first numeric, which is needed when OCR inserts a blank/garbage line between the keyword and the amount.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"xlsx\",\n      \"defect\": \"Strict-schema section describes the None vs '' rule but does not provide an enforced write-time coercion step (e.g., df.where(df.notna() & (df != ''), None) before to_excel) nor a verification assertion that failed-extraction cells are truly empty on re-read.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"repair_recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"change\": \"Rewrite extract_total to collect ALL matches per tier with their line indices, honour EXCLUSIONS first, then within the highest non-empty tier pick the match with the LARGEST line index (bottom-most). Fall back to the next tier only when a tier yields zero matches.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"change\": \"Add an explicit 'post-rounding total' rule: detect lines matching r'ROUND(ING)?(\\\\s*ADJ(USTMENT)?)?' and, when a candidate TOTAL match exists AFTER such a rounding line, prefer it over any TOTAL match that appears before the rounding line (covers 'Total (Inclusive of GST) … Rounding Adj … TOTAL:' receipts).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"change\": \"Extend the two-line fallback to a small forward window (next 2–3 non-empty lines) and strip currency prefixes/noise (RM, :, |, trailing letters) before applying NUM_RE, so garbled-but-aligned amounts are still captured.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"change\": \"Promote extract_date to a keyword-first strategy: first search lines containing DATE / DATED / 'Date :' / 'PRINT DATE' for a date match using DATE_PATTERNS in priority order; only if none are found scan the full text; always prefer the earliest keyed date in reading order, and reject years outside a sensible receipt range (e.g., 2000–2099).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"change\": \"Wire multi_pass_ocr into process_receipt as a retry: if extract_total or extract_date return None, OR if the chosen total disagrees with ≥2 other total-bearing lines (Subtotal+Tax, 'Total Amt Rounded', 'Payment', 'CASH'-'CHANGE') on the same receipt, re-run OCR with alternate PSM/preprocessing variants and re-extract; keep the value that agrees with the most corroborating lines.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"image-ocr\",\n      \"change\": \"Add a short 'receipt field extraction checklist' near the Quality Self-Check section that explicitly calls out: (a) prefer the LAST match in a tier, (b) prefer post-rounding TOTAL, (c) keyword-anchored date, (d) cross-check amount against other total lines, (e) return None (never '', 'nan') on failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"xlsx\",\n      \"change\": \"In the Strict-Schema Outputs section, add an enforced coercion step before to_excel: e.g., `for col in nullable_cols: df[col] = df[col].where(df[col].notna() & (df[col].astype(str).str.len() > 0), None)`, and strengthen the re-read verification to assert that for every row where extraction failed, `pd.isna(cell)` is True (empty cell), not an empty string.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"skill\": \"xlsx\",\n      \"change\": \"Add a one-line reminder in the canonical